<title>USA: Imperial unit files $700 mln shelf offer.</title>
<headline>Imperial unit files $700 mln shelf offer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>ICIFF Secured Assets Corp, a unit of Imperial Credit, filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $700 million in mortgage pass-through certificates.</p>
<p>The certificates will represent an interest in a trust consisting of one to four-family fixed rate first lien mortgages.</p>
<p>The Santa An Heights, Calif. company did not name any underwriters in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
